<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $28.58 bln on June 13.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $28.58 bln on June 13.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $28.58 billion on June 13 from $28.22 billion on June 6, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  June 13     June 6	 June 14</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     24,626	24,262	16,866</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,954	 3,954	 4,509</p>
<p>    SDRs				     3	     3	   212</p>
<p>    Total			     28,583	28,219	21,587</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
